  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8ef4a382a350f98438c21cfd3c789fdf, type: 3}
  m_Name: Net
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonTitle: Net
  lessonId: net
  slides:
  - slideName: Slide 1
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: In this lesson, you will learn about the "net" capture technique, as
      well as ways to escape from it in certain situations.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 2
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Here, black is trying to capture the highlighted white stone.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 3
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Black can attempt to ladder here, but as you can see, white is saved
      by its other stones.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 4
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: To solve this, black places a stone at the highlighted location, forming
      a net-like shape around white.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 5
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: It is now impossible for white to escape. Black captures at the highlighted
      location.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 6
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Netting is only possible when there are stones extruding out both sides
      like these two.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 7
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: If not, white can easily escape and attack black back. Don't let that
      happen!
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 8
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: It is also possible to net groups of two. Try it yourself!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 8e9801a9f9f48024e82879b7cdfe43c0, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 9
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: However, if it is any bigger than two, netting by itself won't work.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 10
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: White escapes by putting black 1 then black 5 in Atari.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 11
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: If the stones on the side are low on liberties, netting won't work
      either. For example, look at the highlighted black stones.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 12
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: As white escapes, they are put in Atari and need to save themselves,
      causing white to escape successfully.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 13
    slideType: 2
    bodyText: Now it's your turn. Can white be net successfully here?
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 14
    slideType: 2
    bodyText: Can white be net successfully here?
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 15
    slideType: 2
    bodyText: Can white be net successfully here?
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 0
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 16
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Avoid being net by white! Remember to use Atari
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 5aca690605f175f41afcd72b1be38482, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 0
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 17
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Nicely done. Come back next time to learn about basic ways to connect
      your stones!
    boardSource: 1
